{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K3WokFprWxLxuZJn2wmkTR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"recency_s025\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"Recency-based eviction (scoring-independent control) at sparsity=0.25, n=100, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B. Tests whether phase gradient remains null at moderate-high sparsity.\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"n_problems\": 100,\n7\t      \"model\": \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B\",\n8\t      \"masking_method\": \"recency\",\n9\t      \"sparsity\": 0.25,\n10\t      \"phase_gradient_median_diff\": 0.032,\n11\t      \"phase_gradient_median_diff_ci95\": [\n12\t        -0.08,\n13\t        0.16\n14\t      ],\n15\t      \"cohens_dz\": 0.14,\n16\t      \"p_value\": 0.38,\n17\t      \"significant\": false,\n18\t      \"low_phase_ii_median\": 0.85,\n19\t      \"high_phase_ii_median\": 0.78,\n20\t      \"low_high_ratio\": 1.09,\n21\t      \"comparison_importance_s025_dz\": 0.95,\n22\t      \"comparison_importance_s025_median_diff\": 3.99,\n23\t      \"importance_vs_recency_ratio\": \"~125×\",\n24\t      \"wilcoxon_p\": 0.38,\n25\t      \"bonferroni_p_k3\": 1.0\n26\t    },\n27\t    \"tables\": [\n28\t      {\n29\t        \"title\": \"Table: Triple dissociation at s025\",\n30\t        \"columns\": [\n31\t          \"Strategy\",\n32\t          \"median_diff\",\n33\t          \"d_z\",\n34\t          \"p\",\n35\t          \"Significant\"\n36\t        ],\n37\t        \"rows\": [\n38\t          [\n39\t            \"Importance\",\n40\t            \"3.99\",\n41\t            \"0.95\",\n42\t            \"<1e-78\",\n43\t            \"Yes\"\n44\t          ],\n45\t          [\n46\t            \"Random\",\n47\t            \"0.26\",\n48\t            \"0.15\",\n49\t            \"0.006 (Bonf.)\",\n50\t            \"Marginal\"\n51\t          ],\n52\t          [\n53\t            \"Recency\",\n54\t            \"0.03\",\n55\t            \"0.14\",\n56\t            \"0.38\",\n57\t            \"No\"\n58\t          ]\n59\t        ]\n60\t      }\n61\t    ],\n62\t    \"figures\": [],\n63\t    \"analysis\": \"s025 结果与 s015 (d_z=0.083) 方向一致：recency 在 moderate sparsity 范围内不产生 显著 phase gradient。d_z 从 0.083 升至 0.14 表明存在微弱的 sparsity-dependent 趋势， 但仍远低于 importance 的 d_z=0.95。Triple dissociation 在 s025 水平进一步确认： phase gradient 是 attention-score mechanism 的特有产物。Random 在 s025 的 marginal significance (n=500 数据 Bonf. p=0.006) 与 recency NS 的对比值得注意——random masking 虽然不使用 importance scores，但其均匀采样仍受 head pruning 后 score distribution 变化的间接影响；recency 完全脱离 score pathway，因此更 clean 作为 control。\\n\\n\\nAt s025, recency eviction removes the oldest 25% of KV entries regardless of attention scores. Since discrimination collapse is driven by importance-score judgment degradation after head pruning, recency eviction bypasses this mechanism entirely. The slight positive trend (d_z=0.14) reflects marginal information loss that differentially affects longer reasoning chains (low-sparsity phase has more accumulated context to lose), but the effect is far below significance. The key mechanistic argument holds: without attention-score-based selection, pruning doesn't create the biased pseudo-random degradation pattern that amplifies compound severity in the low phase. At s025, total information loss from recency eviction is still below the critical threshold where any removal method would trigger phase effects.\\n\"\n64\t  },\n65\t  {\n66\t    \"name\": \"recency_s030\",\n67\t    \"description\": \"Recency-based eviction at sparsity=0.30 (extreme), n=100. Tests whether extreme information loss triggers weak phase-dependent effects even without score-based selection.\\n\",\n68\t    \"results\": {\n69\t      \"n_problems\": 100,\n70\t      \"model\": \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B\",\n71\t      \"masking_method\": \"recency\",\n72\t      \"sparsity\": 0.3,\n73\t      \"phase_gradient_median_diff\": 0.21,\n74\t      \"phase_gradient_median_diff_ci95\": [\n75\t        0.02,\n76\t        0.45\n77\t      ],\n78\t      \"cohens_dz\": 0.32,\n79\t      \"p_value\": 0.028,\n80\t      \"significant_uncorrected\": true,\n81\t      \"significant_bonferroni_k3\": false,\n82\t      \"bonferroni_p\": 0.084,\n83\t      \"low_phase_ii_median\": 1.95,\n84\t      \"high_phase_ii_median\": 1.62,\n85\t      \"low_high_ratio\": 1.2,\n86\t      \"comparison_importance_s030_dz\": 1.13,\n87\t      \"comparison_importance_s030_median_diff\": 8.48,\n88\t      \"importance_vs_recency_dz_ratio\": \"3.5×\",\n89\t      \"importance_vs_recency_mediandiff_ratio\": \"~40×\",\n90\t      \"wilcoxon_p\": 0.028\n91\t    },\n92\t    \"tables\": [\n93\t      {\n94\t        \"title\": \"Table: Triple dissociation at s030\",\n95\t        \"columns\": [\n96\t          \"Strategy\",\n97\t          \"median_diff\",\n98\t          \"d_z\",\n99\t          \"p_uncorrected\",\n100\t          \"p_Bonferroni\",\n101\t          \"Significant\"\n102\t        ],\n103\t        \"rows\": [\n104\t          [\n105\t            \"Importance\",\n106\t            \"8.48\",\n107\t            \"1.13\",\n108\t            \"<1e-79\",\n109\t            \"<1e-79\",\n110\t            \"Yes\"\n111\t          ],\n112\t          [\n113\t            \"Random\",\n114\t            \"0.51\",\n115\t            \"0.35\",\n116\t            \"0.006\",\n117\t            \"0.018\",\n118\t            \"Yes\"\n119\t          ],\n120\t          [\n121\t            \"Recency\",\n122\t            \"0.21\",\n123\t            \"0.32\",\n124\t            \"0.028\",\n125\t            \"0.084\",\n126\t            \"No (trend)\"\n127\t          ]\n128\t        ]\n129\t      },\n130\t      {\n131\t        \"title\": \"Table: Recency d_z dose-response across sparsities\",\n132\t        \"columns\": [\n133\t          \"Sparsity\",\n134\t          \"d_z\",\n135\t          \"p\",\n136\t          \"Interpretation\"\n137\t        ],\n138\t        \"rows\": [\n139\t          [\n140\t            \"s015\",\n141\t            \"0.083\",\n142\t            \"0.77\",\n143\t            \"Null (negligible)\"\n144\t          ],\n145\t          [\n146\t            \"s025\",\n147\t            \"0.14\",\n148\t            \"0.38\",\n149\t            \"Null (negligible)\"\n150\t          ],\n151\t          [\n152\t            \"s030\",\n153\t            \"0.32\",\n154\t            \"0.028\",\n155\t            \"Weak (small, NS after Bonferroni)\"\n156\t          ]\n157\t        ]\n158\t      }\n159\t    ],\n160\t    \"figures\": [],\n161\t    \"analysis\": \"s030 recency 弱信号是 median tier 的定义性特征。关键解读：(1) d_z=0.32 是 small effect，远低于 importance 的 d_z=1.13（3.5× gap）；(2) Bonferroni 校正后 NS，统计 稳健性不足；(3) 机制与 importance 不同——不是 discrimination collapse，而是 information loss 达到临界阈值后 phase-dependent context dependency 的自然反映。 Paper 叙事调整：C11 从 \\\"null at all sparsities\\\" 改为 \\\"null-to-weak, confirming primary mechanism is score-based\\\"。Discussion 新增 paragraph 解释 boundary condition。 Rebuttal 准备：即使 s030 recency 在 larger sample 中确认显著，effect size comparison (importance 40× stronger) 仍然支撑核心 claim。\\n\\n\\nAt extreme sparsity (s030), 30% of attention heads are pruned AND the oldest 30% of KV cache is evicted. Even though recency eviction doesn't use attention scores, the sheer volume of information loss reaches a critical threshold where phase-dependent effects emerge through a different mechanism: low-sparsity phase (reasoning-heavy) relies more heavily on accumulated context from earlier tokens, and recency eviction disproportionately removes this early context. The effect is genuine but weak (d_z=0.32 vs importance d_z=1.13) and fails Bonferroni correction (k=3 strategies tested at s030). This establishes the boundary condition: at extreme sparsity, phase-dependent severity is not exclusively attention-score-driven, but the score-based mechanism remains the dominant driver (~40× stronger in median_diff). The weak recency signal at s030 reflects information-theoretic inevitability rather than the discrimination collapse mechanism.\\n\"\n162\t  },\n163\t  {\n164\t    \"name\": \"gpqa_ds_importance_s020\",\n165\t    \"description\": \"GPQA Diamond benchmark importance masking phase gradient at s=0.20, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B, n≈198. Extends GPQA cross-benchmark validation to second sparsity level.\\n\",\n166\t    \"results\": {\n167\t      \"n_problems\": 198,\n168\t      \"interaction_index\": {\n169\t        \"high\": {\n170\t          \"mean\": 0.58,\n171\t          \"median\": 0.042,\n172\t          \"ci\": [\n173\t            0.21,\n174\t            1.15\n175\t          ],\n176\t          \"median_ci\": [\n177\t            0.035,\n178\t            0.052\n179\t          ],\n180\t          \"winsorized_mean\": 0.18,\n181\t          \"skewness\": 12.5\n182\t        },\n183\t        \"mid\": {\n184\t          \"mean\": 3.25,\n185\t          \"median\": 0.38,\n186\t          \"ci\": [\n187\t            2.45,\n188\t            4.21\n189\t          ],\n190\t          \"median_ci\": [\n191\t            0.32,\n192\t            0.46\n193\t          ],\n194\t          \"winsorized_mean\": 1.85,\n195\t          \"skewness\": 8.2\n196\t        },\n197\t        \"low\": {\n198\t          \"mean\": 18.4,\n199\t          \"median\": 2.85,\n200\t          \"ci\": [\n201\t            15.2,\n202\t            22.1\n203\t          ],\n204\t          \"median_ci\": [\n205\t            2.52,\n206\t            3.25\n207\t          ],\n208\t          \"winsorized_mean\": 12.3,\n209\t          \"skewness\": 7.6\n210\t        }\n211\t      },\n212\t      \"perplexity\": {\n213\t        \"high\": {\n214\t          \"dense\": 1.178,\n215\t          \"attn\": 1.58,\n216\t          \"kv\": 1.92,\n217\t          \"both\": 2.85\n218\t        },\n219\t        \"mid\": {\n220\t          \"dense\": 1.308,\n221\t          \"attn\": 1.74,\n222\t          \"kv\": 4.85,\n223\t          \"both\": 8.12\n224\t        },\n225\t        \"low\": {\n226\t          \"dense\": 1.422,\n227\t          \"attn\": 2.15,\n228\t          \"kv\": 32.5,\n229\t          \"both\": 52.8\n230\t        }\n231\t      },\n232\t      \"phase_stats\": {\n233\t        \"high\": {\n234\t          \"n_tokens\": 479658,\n235\t          \"n_segments\": 6261\n236\t        },\n237\t        \"mid\": {\n238\t          \"n_tokens\": 276409,\n239\t          \"n_segments\": 2185\n240\t        },\n241\t        \"low\": {\n242\t          \"n_tokens\": 465085,\n243\t          \"n_segments\": 5128\n244\t        }\n245\t      },\n246\t      \"pass_fail\": {\n247\t        \"ci_overlap\": true,\n248\t        \"sign_reversal\": false,\n249\t        \"overall\": \"PASS\"\n250\t      },\n251\t      \"gradient_direction\": \"low > mid > high\",\n252\t      \"median_ratio_low_high\": 67.9,\n253\t      \"median_difference\": 2.81,\n254\t      \"wilcoxon_p\": \"<1e-35\",\n255\t      \"cohens_dz\": 0.92\n256\t    },\n257\t    \"tables\": [\n258\t      {\n259\t        \"title\": \"Table: GPQA importance gradient dose-response (DS)\",\n260\t        \"columns\": [\n261\t          \"Sparsity\",\n262\t          \"low_median\",\n263\t          \"high_median\",\n264\t          \"ratio\",\n265\t          \"d_z\",\n266\t          \"p\"\n267\t        ],\n268\t        \"rows\": [\n269\t          [\n270\t            \"s015\",\n271\t            \"0.960\",\n272\t            \"0.013\",\n273\t            \"75.2×\",\n274\t            \"0.81\",\n275\t            \"<1e-29\"\n276\t          ],\n277\t          [\n278\t            \"s020\",\n279\t            \"2.85\",\n280\t            \"0.042\",\n281\t            \"67.9×\",\n282\t            \"0.92\",\n283\t            \"<1e-35\"\n284\t          ]\n285\t        ]\n286\t      }\n287\t    ],\n288\t    \"figures\": [],\n289\t    \"analysis\": \"GPQA s020 确认 phase gradient 在第三个 benchmark 上成立（MATH-500, GSM8K, GPQA）。 Absolute magnitude 高于 MATH-500 同 sparsity (2.85 vs 1.48)，可能因为 GPQA 推理链 更长（更多 tokens 累积 compound interaction）。关键：dose-response monotonicity 跨 benchmark 一致。Strategy specificity ratio 需要对应 GPQA random 实验才能计算； 基于 median tier 预测 ratio 在 2-3× 范围（类似 GSM8K）。\\n\\n\\nGPQA s020 extends the dose-response curve established at s015. From MATH-500 reference, the s015→s020 scaling factor is approximately 3.8× (0.39→1.48). Applying a similar but slightly attenuated ratio to GPQA (given longer reasoning chains and harder problems that may show more gradual scaling): 0.95 × 3.0 ≈ 2.85. GPQA problems elicit longer reasoning chains than MATH-500 (~6000 tokens vs ~1200), meaning more tokens per problem and thus more stable per-problem statistics, but also more opportunity for compound interaction to accumulate. The gradient remains strongly monotonic (high < mid < low) with all phases well-separated. The effect size (d_z ≈ 0.92) places this solidly in the \\\"large\\\" range, consistent with the pattern that phase gradient is robust across benchmarks at the same sparsity level. The per-phase perplexity pattern shows KV-only degradation concentrating in low phase (dense ppl similar across phases, but kv/both ppl diverges dramatically), consistent with discrimination collapse preferentially affecting attention-heavy reasoning segments.\\n\"\n290\t  },\n291\t  {\n292\t    \"name\": \"gpqa_ds_importance_s025\",\n293\t    \"description\": \"GPQA Diamond benchmark importance masking phase gradient at s=0.25, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B, n≈198. Third sparsity level for GPQA dose-response characterization.\\n\",\n294\t    \"results\": {\n295\t      \"n_problems\": 198,\n296\t      \"interaction_index\": {\n297\t        \"high\": {\n298\t          \"mean\": 1.82,\n299\t          \"median\": 0.145,\n300\t          \"ci\": [\n301\t            0.95,\n302\t            3.12\n303\t          ],\n304\t          \"median_ci\": [\n305\t            0.115,\n306\t            0.185\n307\t          ],\n308\t          \"winsorized_mean\": 0.72,\n309\t          \"skewness\": 10.8\n310\t        },\n311\t        \"mid\": {\n312\t          \"mean\": 12.5,\n313\t          \"median\": 1.65,\n314\t          \"ci\": [\n315\t            8.8,\n316\t            17.2\n317\t          ],\n318\t          \"median_ci\": [\n319\t            1.35,\n320\t            2.05\n321\t          ],\n322\t          \"winsorized_mean\": 7.8,\n323\t          \"skewness\": 8.9\n324\t        },\n325\t        \"low\": {\n326\t          \"mean\": 52.3,\n327\t          \"median\": 8.2,\n328\t          \"ci\": [\n329\t            40.5,\n330\t            66.8\n331\t          ],\n332\t          \"median_ci\": [\n333\t            7.1,\n334\t            9.5\n335\t          ],\n336\t          \"winsorized_mean\": 35.6,\n337\t          \"skewness\": 7.2\n338\t        }\n339\t      },\n340\t      \"perplexity\": {\n341\t        \"high\": {\n342\t          \"dense\": 1.178,\n343\t          \"attn\": 1.72,\n344\t          \"kv\": 2.35,\n345\t          \"both\": 4.15\n346\t        },\n347\t        \"mid\": {\n348\t          \"dense\": 1.308,\n349\t          \"attn\": 1.92,\n350\t          \"kv\": 8.5,\n351\t          \"both\": 18.6\n352\t        },\n353\t        \"low\": {\n354\t          \"dense\": 1.422,\n355\t          \"attn\": 2.45,\n356\t          \"kv\": 55.2,\n357\t          \"both\": 98.5\n358\t        }\n359\t      },\n360\t      \"phase_stats\": {\n361\t        \"high\": {\n362\t          \"n_tokens\": 479658,\n363\t          \"n_segments\": 6261\n364\t        },\n365\t        \"mid\": {\n366\t          \"n_tokens\": 276409,\n367\t          \"n_segments\": 2185\n368\t        },\n369\t        \"low\": {\n370\t          \"n_tokens\": 465085,\n371\t          \"n_segments\": 5128\n372\t        }\n373\t      },\n374\t      \"pass_fail\": {\n375\t        \"ci_overlap\": true,\n376\t        \"sign_reversal\": false,\n377\t        \"overall\": \"PASS\"\n378\t      },\n379\t      \"gradient_direction\": \"low > mid > high\",\n380\t      \"median_ratio_low_high\": 56.6,\n381\t      \"median_difference\": 8.06,\n382\t      \"wilcoxon_p\": \"<1e-42\",\n383\t      \"cohens_dz\": 1.05,\n384\t      \"gpqa_strategy_specificity_ratio_estimated\": 2.5\n385\t    },\n386\t    \"tables\": [\n387\t      {\n388\t        \"title\": \"Table: GPQA full dose-response (importance, DS)\",\n389\t        \"columns\": [\n390\t          \"Sparsity\",\n391\t          \"low_median\",\n392\t          \"mid_median\",\n393\t          \"high_median\",\n394\t          \"gradient\",\n395\t          \"d_z\"\n396\t        ],\n397\t        \"rows\": [\n398\t          [\n399\t            \"s015\",\n400\t            \"0.960\",\n401\t            \"0.102\",\n402\t            \"0.013\",\n403\t            \"0.947\",\n404\t            \"0.81\"\n405\t          ],\n406\t          [\n407\t            \"s020\",\n408\t            \"2.85\",\n409\t            \"0.38\",\n410\t            \"0.042\",\n411\t            \"2.81\",\n412\t            \"0.92\"\n413\t          ],\n414\t          [\n415\t            \"s025\",\n416\t            \"8.20\",\n417\t            \"1.65\",\n418\t            \"0.145\",\n419\t            \"8.06\",\n420\t            \"1.05\"\n421\t          ]\n422\t        ]\n423\t      },\n424\t      {\n425\t        \"title\": \"Table: Cross-benchmark strategy specificity ratio comparison\",\n426\t        \"columns\": [\n427\t          \"Benchmark\",\n428\t          \"s025 imp/rand ratio\",\n429\t          \"Task complexity\"\n430\t        ],\n431\t        \"rows\": [\n432\t          [\n433\t            \"MATH-500\",\n434\t            \"15.5×\",\n435\t            \"Medium (short chains)\"\n436\t          ],\n437\t          [\n438\t            \"GSM8K\",\n439\t            \"3.8×\",\n440\t            \"Low (very short chains)\"\n441\t          ],\n442\t          [\n443\t            \"GPQA\",\n444\t            \"~2.5×\",\n445\t            \"High (long chains)\"\n446\t          ]\n447\t        ]\n448\t      }\n449\t    ],\n450\t    \"figures\": [],\n451\t    \"analysis\": \"GPQA s025 完成三点 dose-response，确认跨 benchmark monotonicity。关键发现： (1) Gradient magnitude 高于 MATH-500 (8.06 vs 7.16 at s025)——更长推理链累积更多 compound interaction；(2) Strategy specificity ratio (~2.5×) 继续 GSM8K 的衰减趋势， 进一步确认 task-modulation；(3) 低 ratio 的机制解释：GPQA 推理链长(~6000 tokens)， 即使 random eviction 也在 longer chains 上产生 moderate phase gradient，压缩了 imp/rand gap。这为 reviewer 提供了清晰的 task-dependence 故事：chain length 调制 strategy specificity 强度，而 phase gradient 本身跨 task 稳健。 C1 claim 最终形式：strategy specificity 是 task-modulated second-order finding， 不是 universal constant。\\n\\n\\nAt s025, GPQA follows the same dose-response escalation pattern. From s020→s025 in MATH-500, the scaling factor is 4.8× (1.48→7.16). For GPQA, applying a modestly attenuated ratio (~2.8×) given the already-high baseline: 2.85 × 2.8 ≈ 8.0. The attenuation reflects a ceiling effect as reasoning chains at GPQA difficulty level experience compound degradation more uniformly (the most complex reasoning steps are already heavily impacted at s020). The low/high ratio decreases slightly from 75× (s015) to 68× (s020) to 57× (s025) as high-phase II starts rising from its near-zero baseline. This mirrors MATH-500 where the ratio also peaks at lower sparsity. The d_z=1.05 (large) confirms that even at higher sparsity, the phase-dependent signal remains extremely robust on GPQA. For strategy specificity, based on the median tier and GSM8K precedent: GPQA imp/rand ratio is estimated at 2-3× (predicting ~2.5×), far below MATH-500's 15-17× but consistent with the task-modulation narrative. Harder tasks with longer reasoning chains show weaker strategy specificity because even random eviction becomes increasingly damaging in a phase-dependent manner when chains are long.\\n\"\n452\t  },\n453\t  {\n454\t    \"name\": \"gpqa_random_s025_predicted\",\n455\t    \"description\": \"Predicted GPQA random masking result needed to compute strategy specificity ratio. Not currently in registry but implied by median tier requiring imp/rand ratio calculation.\\n\",\n456\t    \"results\": {\n457\t      \"n_problems\": 198,\n458\t      \"low_phase_ii_median\": 4.2,\n459\t      \"high_phase_ii_median\": 1.35,\n460\t      \"median_gradient\": 2.85,\n461\t      \"median_gradient_ci\": [\n462\t        1.8,\n463\t        4.1\n464\t      ],\n465\t      \"cohens_dz\": 0.38,\n466\t      \"wilcoxon_p\": 0.0015,\n467\t      \"imp_rand_ratio_s025\": 2.83\n468\t    },\n469\t    \"tables\": [],\n470\t    \"figures\": [],\n471\t    \"analysis\": \"Strategy specificity ratio 在 GPQA 上的衰减 (2.8× vs MATH-500 的 15.5×) 是 median tier 的核心预测之一。机制：task complexity → chain length → random eviction 也产生 significant phase gradient → ratio 压缩。这不是 importance eviction 变弱 （GPQA importance gradient 实际更强），而是 random eviction 在长链上变强。 Reviewer 可能质疑：如果 random 也显著，specificity claim 是否成立？ Rebuttal：specificity 不是 binary (significant vs not)，而是 graded — importance consistently 2-3× stronger across all tested benchmarks，且在短链 benchmarks (MATH) 上 specificity 极强 (15×)。\\n\\n\\nGPQA random masking at s025 is predicted to show a moderate phase gradient (d_z≈0.38, significant) because: (1) GPQA's long reasoning chains mean even random token removal has phase-dependent impact (more accumulated context in low phase = more to lose); (2) this parallels GSM8K where random is significant at s025 (QW: d_z≈0.16 with ratio 3.8×); (3) GPQA's longer chains amplify the random effect more than MATH-500. The resulting imp/rand ratio of ~2.8× fits squarely in the median tier's predicted [1.8, 3.5] range and reinforces the narrative that strategy specificity is task-complexity-modulated.\\n\"\n472\t  },\n473\t  {\n474\t    \"name\": \"c9_literature_differentiation\",\n475\t    \"description\": \"Non-experimental claim. Differentiation from Lethe/SparK/ThinKV/Physics-of-KV through Related Work positioning.\\n\",\n476\t    \"results\": {\n477\t      \"type\": \"literature_review\",\n478\t      \"status\": \"addressed_in_paper\",\n479\t      \"key_distinctions\": {\n480\t        \"vs_lethe\": \"Method paper (adaptive eviction) vs empirical finding (phase-dependent severity)\",\n481\t        \"vs_spark\": \"Treats compound interaction as uniform; we show it's phase×strategy modulated\",\n482\t        \"vs_thinkv\": \"Single-axis phase-aware compression; we study dual-axis compound interaction\",\n483\t        \"vs_physics_kv\": \"Single-axis compression-rate phase transition; we study reasoning-phase modulation\",\n484\t        \"vs_hies\": \"Single-axis score collapse observation; we show compound amplification of collapse\",\n485\t        \"vs_rkv\": \"Task-specific optimization method; we do mechanistic analysis\"\n486\t      },\n487\t      \"citation_count_target\": \"≥50 (currently met)\"\n488\t    },\n489\t    \"tables\": [],\n490\t    \"figures\": [],\n491\t    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 对 novelty 的 median 评分 (2.8-3.3) 反映了一个现实：empirical finding paper 在 novelty 维度天然弱于 method paper。应对策略：(1) 强调 no prior work 同时分析 compound × phase × strategy 三维交互；(2) C11 的 recency control 作为 experimental design novelty 是独特贡献（\\\"repurposing recency eviction as methodological control has no precedent\\\"）；(3) crossover phenomenon (C3) 是 全新发现，prior work 无法预测。\\n\\n\\nC9 不需要新实验——通过 Related Work §2 的结构化比较和 gap analysis 完成。Median tier 下 reviewer 可能仍认为 novelty 偏窄（\\\"incremental over existing phase-aware methods\\\"）， reviewer_novelty_score 预期 2.8-3.3。应对：强调 experimental design contribution (recency as methodological control) 和 three-way interaction 的发现性质。\\n\"\n492\t  }\n493\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a4d7a49-50e1-4fc9-a56f-f940b6dbf598","uuid":"073e8f62-9097-4bfc-9f58-28e6faf80c6a","timestamp":"2026-05-17T01:13:02.895Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_11/projects/phase-gated-compound-sparse/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260517T005655/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"recency_s025\",\n    \"description\": \"Recency-based eviction (scoring-independent control) at sparsity=0.25, n=100, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B. Tests whether phase gradient remains null at moderate-high sparsity.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_problems\": 100,\n      \"model\": \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B\",\n      \"masking_method\": \"recency\",\n      \"sparsity\": 0.25,\n      \"phase_gradient_median_diff\": 0.032,\n      \"phase_gradient_median_diff_ci95\": [\n        -0.08,\n        0.16\n      ],\n      \"cohens_dz\": 0.14,\n      \"p_value\": 0.38,\n      \"significant\": false,\n      \"low_phase_ii_median\": 0.85,\n      \"high_phase_ii_median\": 0.78,\n      \"low_high_ratio\": 1.09,\n      \"comparison_importance_s025_dz\": 0.95,\n      \"comparison_importance_s025_median_diff\": 3.99,\n      \"importance_vs_recency_ratio\": \"~125×\",\n      \"wilcoxon_p\": 0.38,\n      \"bonferroni_p_k3\": 1.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Triple dissociation at s025\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Strategy\",\n          \"median_diff\",\n          \"d_z\",\n          \"p\",\n          \"Significant\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Importance\",\n            \"3.99\",\n            \"0.95\",\n            \"<1e-78\",\n            \"Yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random\",\n            \"0.26\",\n            \"0.15\",\n            \"0.006 (Bonf.)\",\n            \"Marginal\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Recency\",\n            \"0.03\",\n            \"0.14\",\n            \"0.38\",\n            \"No\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"s025 结果与 s015 (d_z=0.083) 方向一致：recency 在 moderate sparsity 范围内不产生 显著 phase gradient。d_z 从 0.083 升至 0.14 表明存在微弱的 sparsity-dependent 趋势， 但仍远低于 importance 的 d_z=0.95。Triple dissociation 在 s025 水平进一步确认： phase gradient 是 attention-score mechanism 的特有产物。Random 在 s025 的 marginal significance (n=500 数据 Bonf. p=0.006) 与 recency NS 的对比值得注意——random masking 虽然不使用 importance scores，但其均匀采样仍受 head pruning 后 score distribution 变化的间接影响；recency 完全脱离 score pathway，因此更 clean 作为 control。\\n\\n\\nAt s025, recency eviction removes the oldest 25% of KV entries regardless of attention scores. Since discrimination collapse is driven by importance-score judgment degradation after head pruning, recency eviction bypasses this mechanism entirely. The slight positive trend (d_z=0.14) reflects marginal information loss that differentially affects longer reasoning chains (low-sparsity phase has more accumulated context to lose), but the effect is far below significance. The key mechanistic argument holds: without attention-score-based selection, pruning doesn't create the biased pseudo-random degradation pattern that amplifies compound severity in the low phase. At s025, total information loss from recency eviction is still below the critical threshold where any removal method would trigger phase effects.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"recency_s030\",\n    \"description\": \"Recency-based eviction at sparsity=0.30 (extreme), n=100. Tests whether extreme information loss triggers weak phase-dependent effects even without score-based selection.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_problems\": 100,\n      \"model\": \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B\",\n      \"masking_method\": \"recency\",\n      \"sparsity\": 0.3,\n      \"phase_gradient_median_diff\": 0.21,\n      \"phase_gradient_median_diff_ci95\": [\n        0.02,\n        0.45\n      ],\n      \"cohens_dz\": 0.32,\n      \"p_value\": 0.028,\n      \"significant_uncorrected\": true,\n      \"significant_bonferroni_k3\": false,\n      \"bonferroni_p\": 0.084,\n      \"low_phase_ii_median\": 1.95,\n      \"high_phase_ii_median\": 1.62,\n      \"low_high_ratio\": 1.2,\n      \"comparison_importance_s030_dz\": 1.13,\n      \"comparison_importance_s030_median_diff\": 8.48,\n      \"importance_vs_recency_dz_ratio\": \"3.5×\",\n      \"importance_vs_recency_mediandiff_ratio\": \"~40×\",\n      \"wilcoxon_p\": 0.028\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Triple dissociation at s030\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Strategy\",\n          \"median_diff\",\n          \"d_z\",\n          \"p_uncorrected\",\n          \"p_Bonferroni\",\n          \"Significant\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Importance\",\n            \"8.48\",\n            \"1.13\",\n            \"<1e-79\",\n            \"<1e-79\",\n            \"Yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random\",\n            \"0.51\",\n            \"0.35\",\n            \"0.006\",\n            \"0.018\",\n            \"Yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Recency\",\n            \"0.21\",\n            \"0.32\",\n            \"0.028\",\n            \"0.084\",\n            \"No (trend)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Recency d_z dose-response across sparsities\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Sparsity\",\n          \"d_z\",\n          \"p\",\n          \"Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"s015\",\n            \"0.083\",\n            \"0.77\",\n            \"Null (negligible)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"s025\",\n            \"0.14\",\n            \"0.38\",\n            \"Null (negligible)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"s030\",\n            \"0.32\",\n            \"0.028\",\n            \"Weak (small, NS after Bonferroni)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"s030 recency 弱信号是 median tier 的定义性特征。关键解读：(1) d_z=0.32 是 small effect，远低于 importance 的 d_z=1.13（3.5× gap）；(2) Bonferroni 校正后 NS，统计 稳健性不足；(3) 机制与 importance 不同——不是 discrimination collapse，而是 information loss 达到临界阈值后 phase-dependent context dependency 的自然反映。 Paper 叙事调整：C11 从 \\\"null at all sparsities\\\" 改为 \\\"null-to-weak, confirming primary mechanism is score-based\\\"。Discussion 新增 paragraph 解释 boundary condition。 Rebuttal 准备：即使 s030 recency 在 larger sample 中确认显著，effect size comparison (importance 40× stronger) 仍然支撑核心 claim。\\n\\n\\nAt extreme sparsity (s030), 30% of attention heads are pruned AND the oldest 30% of KV cache is evicted. Even though recency eviction doesn't use attention scores, the sheer volume of information loss reaches a critical threshold where phase-dependent effects emerge through a different mechanism: low-sparsity phase (reasoning-heavy) relies more heavily on accumulated context from earlier tokens, and recency eviction disproportionately removes this early context. The effect is genuine but weak (d_z=0.32 vs importance d_z=1.13) and fails Bonferroni correction (k=3 strategies tested at s030). This establishes the boundary condition: at extreme sparsity, phase-dependent severity is not exclusively attention-score-driven, but the score-based mechanism remains the dominant driver (~40× stronger in median_diff). The weak recency signal at s030 reflects information-theoretic inevitability rather than the discrimination collapse mechanism.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"gpqa_ds_importance_s020\",\n    \"description\": \"GPQA Diamond benchmark importance masking phase gradient at s=0.20, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B, n≈198. Extends GPQA cross-benchmark validation to second sparsity level.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_problems\": 198,\n      \"interaction_index\": {\n        \"high\": {\n          \"mean\": 0.58,\n          \"median\": 0.042,\n          \"ci\": [\n            0.21,\n            1.15\n          ],\n          \"median_ci\": [\n            0.035,\n            0.052\n          ],\n          \"winsorized_mean\": 0.18,\n          \"skewness\": 12.5\n        },\n        \"mid\": {\n          \"mean\": 3.25,\n          \"median\": 0.38,\n          \"ci\": [\n            2.45,\n            4.21\n          ],\n          \"median_ci\": [\n            0.32,\n            0.46\n          ],\n          \"winsorized_mean\": 1.85,\n          \"skewness\": 8.2\n        },\n        \"low\": {\n          \"mean\": 18.4,\n          \"median\": 2.85,\n          \"ci\": [\n            15.2,\n            22.1\n          ],\n          \"median_ci\": [\n            2.52,\n            3.25\n          ],\n          \"winsorized_mean\": 12.3,\n          \"skewness\": 7.6\n        }\n      },\n      \"perplexity\": {\n        \"high\": {\n          \"dense\": 1.178,\n          \"attn\": 1.58,\n          \"kv\": 1.92,\n          \"both\": 2.85\n        },\n        \"mid\": {\n          \"dense\": 1.308,\n          \"attn\": 1.74,\n          \"kv\": 4.85,\n          \"both\": 8.12\n        },\n        \"low\": {\n          \"dense\": 1.422,\n          \"attn\": 2.15,\n          \"kv\": 32.5,\n          \"both\": 52.8\n        }\n      },\n      \"phase_stats\": {\n        \"high\": {\n          \"n_tokens\": 479658,\n          \"n_segments\": 6261\n        },\n        \"mid\": {\n          \"n_tokens\": 276409,\n          \"n_segments\": 2185\n        },\n        \"low\": {\n          \"n_tokens\": 465085,\n          \"n_segments\": 5128\n        }\n      },\n      \"pass_fail\": {\n        \"ci_overlap\": true,\n        \"sign_reversal\": false,\n        \"overall\": \"PASS\"\n      },\n      \"gradient_direction\": \"low > mid > high\",\n      \"median_ratio_low_high\": 67.9,\n      \"median_difference\": 2.81,\n      \"wilcoxon_p\": \"<1e-35\",\n      \"cohens_dz\": 0.92\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: GPQA importance gradient dose-response (DS)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Sparsity\",\n          \"low_median\",\n          \"high_median\",\n          \"ratio\",\n          \"d_z\",\n          \"p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"s015\",\n            \"0.960\",\n            \"0.013\",\n            \"75.2×\",\n            \"0.81\",\n            \"<1e-29\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"s020\",\n            \"2.85\",\n            \"0.042\",\n            \"67.9×\",\n            \"0.92\",\n            \"<1e-35\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"GPQA s020 确认 phase gradient 在第三个 benchmark 上成立（MATH-500, GSM8K, GPQA）。 Absolute magnitude 高于 MATH-500 同 sparsity (2.85 vs 1.48)，可能因为 GPQA 推理链 更长（更多 tokens 累积 compound interaction）。关键：dose-response monotonicity 跨 benchmark 一致。Strategy specificity ratio 需要对应 GPQA random 实验才能计算； 基于 median tier 预测 ratio 在 2-3× 范围（类似 GSM8K）。\\n\\n\\nGPQA s020 extends the dose-response curve established at s015. From MATH-500 reference, the s015→s020 scaling factor is approximately 3.8× (0.39→1.48). Applying a similar but slightly attenuated ratio to GPQA (given longer reasoning chains and harder problems that may show more gradual scaling): 0.95 × 3.0 ≈ 2.85. GPQA problems elicit longer reasoning chains than MATH-500 (~6000 tokens vs ~1200), meaning more tokens per problem and thus more stable per-problem statistics, but also more opportunity for compound interaction to accumulate. The gradient remains strongly monotonic (high < mid < low) with all phases well-separated. The effect size (d_z ≈ 0.92) places this solidly in the \\\"large\\\" range, consistent with the pattern that phase gradient is robust across benchmarks at the same sparsity level. The per-phase perplexity pattern shows KV-only degradation concentrating in low phase (dense ppl similar across phases, but kv/both ppl diverges dramatically), consistent with discrimination collapse preferentially affecting attention-heavy reasoning segments.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"gpqa_ds_importance_s025\",\n    \"description\": \"GPQA Diamond benchmark importance masking phase gradient at s=0.25, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B, n≈198. Third sparsity level for GPQA dose-response characterization.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_problems\": 198,\n      \"interaction_index\": {\n        \"high\": {\n          \"mean\": 1.82,\n          \"median\": 0.145,\n          \"ci\": [\n            0.95,\n            3.12\n          ],\n          \"median_ci\": [\n            0.115,\n            0.185\n          ],\n          \"winsorized_mean\": 0.72,\n          \"skewness\": 10.8\n        },\n        \"mid\": {\n          \"mean\": 12.5,\n          \"median\": 1.65,\n          \"ci\": [\n            8.8,\n            17.2\n          ],\n          \"median_ci\": [\n            1.35,\n            2.05\n          ],\n          \"winsorized_mean\": 7.8,\n          \"skewness\": 8.9\n        },\n        \"low\": {\n          \"mean\": 52.3,\n          \"median\": 8.2,\n          \"ci\": [\n            40.5,\n            66.8\n          ],\n          \"median_ci\": [\n            7.1,\n            9.5\n          ],\n          \"winsorized_mean\": 35.6,\n          \"skewness\": 7.2\n        }\n      },\n      \"perplexity\": {\n        \"high\": {\n          \"dense\": 1.178,\n          \"attn\": 1.72,\n          \"kv\": 2.35,\n          \"both\": 4.15\n        },\n        \"mid\": {\n          \"dense\": 1.308,\n          \"attn\": 1.92,\n          \"kv\": 8.5,\n          \"both\": 18.6\n        },\n        \"low\": {\n          \"dense\": 1.422,\n          \"attn\": 2.45,\n          \"kv\": 55.2,\n          \"both\": 98.5\n        }\n      },\n      \"phase_stats\": {\n        \"high\": {\n          \"n_tokens\": 479658,\n          \"n_segments\": 6261\n        },\n        \"mid\": {\n          \"n_tokens\": 276409,\n          \"n_segments\": 2185\n        },\n        \"low\": {\n          \"n_tokens\": 465085,\n          \"n_segments\": 5128\n        }\n      },\n      \"pass_fail\": {\n        \"ci_overlap\": true,\n        \"sign_reversal\": false,\n        \"overall\": \"PASS\"\n      },\n      \"gradient_direction\": \"low > mid > high\",\n      \"median_ratio_low_high\": 56.6,\n      \"median_difference\": 8.06,\n      \"wilcoxon_p\": \"<1e-42\",\n      \"cohens_dz\": 1.05,\n      \"gpqa_strategy_specificity_ratio_estimated\": 2.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: GPQA full dose-response (importance, DS)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Sparsity\",\n          \"low_median\",\n          \"mid_median\",\n          \"high_median\",\n          \"gradient\",\n          \"d_z\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"s015\",\n            \"0.960\",\n            \"0.102\",\n            \"0.013\",\n            \"0.947\",\n            \"0.81\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"s020\",\n            \"2.85\",\n            \"0.38\",\n            \"0.042\",\n            \"2.81\",\n            \"0.92\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"s025\",\n            \"8.20\",\n            \"1.65\",\n            \"0.145\",\n            \"8.06\",\n            \"1.05\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Cross-benchmark strategy specificity ratio comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"s025 imp/rand ratio\",\n          \"Task complexity\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MATH-500\",\n            \"15.5×\",\n            \"Medium (short chains)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            \"3.8×\",\n            \"Low (very short chains)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPQA\",\n            \"~2.5×\",\n            \"High (long chains)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"GPQA s025 完成三点 dose-response，确认跨 benchmark monotonicity。关键发现： (1) Gradient magnitude 高于 MATH-500 (8.06 vs 7.16 at s025)——更长推理链累积更多 compound interaction；(2) Strategy specificity ratio (~2.5×) 继续 GSM8K 的衰减趋势， 进一步确认 task-modulation；(3) 低 ratio 的机制解释：GPQA 推理链长(~6000 tokens)， 即使 random eviction 也在 longer chains 上产生 moderate phase gradient，压缩了 imp/rand gap。这为 reviewer 提供了清晰的 task-dependence 故事：chain length 调制 strategy specificity 强度，而 phase gradient 本身跨 task 稳健。 C1 claim 最终形式：strategy specificity 是 task-modulated second-order finding， 不是 universal constant。\\n\\n\\nAt s025, GPQA follows the same dose-response escalation pattern. From s020→s025 in MATH-500, the scaling factor is 4.8× (1.48→7.16). For GPQA, applying a modestly attenuated ratio (~2.8×) given the already-high baseline: 2.85 × 2.8 ≈ 8.0. The attenuation reflects a ceiling effect as reasoning chains at GPQA difficulty level experience compound degradation more uniformly (the most complex reasoning steps are already heavily impacted at s020). The low/high ratio decreases slightly from 75× (s015) to 68× (s020) to 57× (s025) as high-phase II starts rising from its near-zero baseline. This mirrors MATH-500 where the ratio also peaks at lower sparsity. The d_z=1.05 (large) confirms that even at higher sparsity, the phase-dependent signal remains extremely robust on GPQA. For strategy specificity, based on the median tier and GSM8K precedent: GPQA imp/rand ratio is estimated at 2-3× (predicting ~2.5×), far below MATH-500's 15-17× but consistent with the task-modulation narrative. Harder tasks with longer reasoning chains show weaker strategy specificity because even random eviction becomes increasingly damaging in a phase-dependent manner when chains are long.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"gpqa_random_s025_predicted\",\n    \"description\": \"Predicted GPQA random masking result needed to compute strategy specificity ratio. Not currently in registry but implied by median tier requiring imp/rand ratio calculation.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_problems\": 198,\n      \"low_phase_ii_median\": 4.2,\n      \"high_phase_ii_median\": 1.35,\n      \"median_gradient\": 2.85,\n      \"median_gradient_ci\": [\n        1.8,\n        4.1\n      ],\n      \"cohens_dz\": 0.38,\n      \"wilcoxon_p\": 0.0015,\n      \"imp_rand_ratio_s025\": 2.83\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Strategy specificity ratio 在 GPQA 上的衰减 (2.8× vs MATH-500 的 15.5×) 是 median tier 的核心预测之一。机制：task complexity → chain length → random eviction 也产生 significant phase gradient → ratio 压缩。这不是 importance eviction 变弱 （GPQA importance gradient 实际更强），而是 random eviction 在长链上变强。 Reviewer 可能质疑：如果 random 也显著，specificity claim 是否成立？ Rebuttal：specificity 不是 binary (significant vs not)，而是 graded — importance consistently 2-3× stronger across all tested benchmarks，且在短链 benchmarks (MATH) 上 specificity 极强 (15×)。\\n\\n\\nGPQA random masking at s025 is predicted to show a moderate phase gradient (d_z≈0.38, significant) because: (1) GPQA's long reasoning chains mean even random token removal has phase-dependent impact (more accumulated context in low phase = more to lose); (2) this parallels GSM8K where random is significant at s025 (QW: d_z≈0.16 with ratio 3.8×); (3) GPQA's longer chains amplify the random effect more than MATH-500. The resulting imp/rand ratio of ~2.8× fits squarely in the median tier's predicted [1.8, 3.5] range and reinforces the narrative that strategy specificity is task-complexity-modulated.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"c9_literature_differentiation\",\n    \"description\": \"Non-experimental claim. Differentiation from Lethe/SparK/ThinKV/Physics-of-KV through Related Work positioning.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"type\": \"literature_review\",\n      \"status\": \"addressed_in_paper\",\n      \"key_distinctions\": {\n        \"vs_lethe\": \"Method paper (adaptive eviction) vs empirical finding (phase-dependent severity)\",\n        \"vs_spark\": \"Treats compound interaction as uniform; we show it's phase×strategy modulated\",\n        \"vs_thinkv\": \"Single-axis phase-aware compression; we study dual-axis compound interaction\",\n        \"vs_physics_kv\": \"Single-axis compression-rate phase transition; we study reasoning-phase modulation\",\n        \"vs_hies\": \"Single-axis score collapse observation; we show compound amplification of collapse\",\n        \"vs_rkv\": \"Task-specific optimization method; we do mechanistic analysis\"\n      },\n      \"citation_count_target\": \"≥50 (currently met)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 对 novelty 的 median 评分 (2.8-3.3) 反映了一个现实：empirical finding paper 在 novelty 维度天然弱于 method paper。应对策略：(1) 强调 no prior work 同时分析 compound × phase × strategy 三维交互；(2) C11 的 recency control 作为 experimental design novelty 是独特贡献（\\\"repurposing recency eviction as methodological control has no precedent\\\"）；(3) crossover phenomenon (C3) 是 全新发现，prior work 无法预测。\\n\\n\\nC9 不需要新实验——通过 Related Work §2 的结构化比较和 gap analysis 完成。Median tier 下 reviewer 可能仍认为 novelty 偏窄（\\\"incremental over existing phase-aware methods\\\"）， reviewer_novelty_score 预期 2.8-3.3。应对：强调 experimental design contribution (recency as methodological control) 和 three-way interaction 的发现性质。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":493,"startLine":1,"totalLines":493}}}
